Linux CLI:
1. grep "search keyword" file name
grep -E "value1|value2|value3|" file name
2. wc -l file name for the amount of entries in the file
3. find -name filename and find -name *.fileformat
4. & to run the command in the background
5. && to chain the commands, coomand1 && command2, command2 will be only executed if command1 is successfull
6. echo "textvalue > filename - replace the txt in the file
7. echo "textvalue" >> filename - add text to the file 
8. ssh accountusername@IP -> enter the password to connect to the remote machine
9. touch name of the file - to create a file
10. mkdir to create directory
11. rm filename or rm -R directory name to remove file or directory
12. mv filename1 filename2 - rename the filename1 and merge the content filename2
13. file filename - to know the file extension
14. su account name
15. ls -lh to check permisssions 
r = 4
w = 2
e = 1 
777 = full access for owner, group and others

Active Directory
mstsc /v:ip address, to access remote machine after the delegation done
